From: Androlinzberg maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] HWUI: reject pixel copy when Surface has no native window

The hosted renderer obtains its render target directly and cannot translate a
Java Surface to ANativeWindow. Complete PixelCopy with the stock SourceInvalid
result instead of dereferencing a null window in RenderProxy. Java retains its
validation and callback executor/Handler behavior; this adds no presentation or
buffer-copy backend.

diff --git a/libs/hwui/jni/android_graphics_HardwareRenderer.cpp b/libs/hwui/jni/android_graphics_HardwareRenderer.cpp
--- a/libs/hwui/jni/android_graphics_HardwareRenderer.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/jni/android_graphics_HardwareRenderer.cpp
@@ -717,6 +717,10 @@
             vm, env->NewGlobalRef(jCopyRequest),
             ::android::uirenderer::Rect(left, top, right, bottom));
     ANativeWindow* window = fromSurface(env, jsurface);
+    if (window == nullptr) {
+        copyRequest->onCopyFinished(CopyResult::SourceInvalid);
+        return;
+    }
     RenderProxy::copySurfaceInto(window, std::move(copyRequest));
     ANativeWindow_release(window);
 }
